 r←AssertedFrom;i;names;helpers;prefix
⍝ 'name[line]' of where the assertion was made: the line of the test function (test_...) on the stack, which says which
⍝ of its many assertions failed also when it went through assertError or a helper of its own such as assert_create;
⍝ or, off a test (e.g. RunTestThread), the nearest function that is not one of the assertion helpers
 names←1↓⎕XSI ⍝ without this function
 prefix←(⍕⎕THIS),'.test_'
 i←1⍳⍨(⊂prefix)≡¨(≢prefix)↑¨names
 :If i>≢names
     helpers←(⊂(⍕⎕THIS),'.'),¨'assert' 'assertError' 'assertMsg' 'AssertFailed'
     i←1⍳⍨~names∊helpers
 :EndIf
 r←(i⊃names),'[',(⍕i⊃1↓⎕LC),']'
